course: dictionary
lesson: 1507
title: Celebrity: famous people and fame
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A celebrity is a famous person, often in films, music, sport or TV. Celebrity can also mean fame itself: the state of being famous. Informal writers may shorten it to celeb.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Become a celebrity» means to start being famous. «A celebrity chef» is a famous cook, and the word before celebrity tells you what the person is famous for.
explain: Being famous does not make someone a reliable source. «Celebrity feuds» may be real, exaggerated or staged for publicity, and fans who take sides often do not know the stars at all. So ask yourself: how do I know this is true?
fact: A celebrity is a famous person, especially in films, music, sport or TV.
fact: Celebrity can also mean the state of being famous.
fact: Celeb is an informal, shortened way to say celebrity.
fact: «Celebrity death hoaxes» are fake stories that a famous person has died, so wait for trusted news before sharing.
fact: Photos of celebrities are often edited, and some accounts pretending to be celebrities are fake.
exercise: «Become a celebrity» means what? | To learn how to cook well | To buy a brand new phone | *To start being famous | Stop going out and stay at home
exercise: Nadia says, «Celeb is a silly word for a cook.» Who is a celeb? | A person who sells fresh fruit | *A famous person, such as a film star or singer | A kind of cook in the kitchen
exercise: Before sharing news that a famous person has died, what should you do? | Ask the celebrity's friends in the street | *Wait for trusted news or the person's official account | Post it with a laughing emoji | Share it quickly before anyone else does
test: Which word means the state of being famous? | Compass | Cushion | Courage | *Celebrity
test: Which is true about a photo of a celebrity online? | It is always a true, unedited picture | *It may have been edited | It can never be shared with friends
exam: Which phrase uses celebrity to mean a famous person? | Hiding under the old bridge | *A celebrity guest on the show | A bowl of warm soup | Feeling cold on a winter walk
